<title>USA: N.J. Senate expected to pass toll bill -- paper.</title>
<headline>N.J. Senate expected to pass toll bill -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Jersey Senate is expected Monday to pass a bill to finance a $400 million electronic toll collection project, the Star Ledger reported Monday.</p>
<p>The bill would use cameras and computer enforcement methods to charge toll evaders a $25 fine, with revenues used to finance a new electronic toll collection system on the state's major highways.</p>
<p>If approved by the state Assembly, such a system could be in place by mid-1998.</p>
<p>The contract for the toll collection system is expected to be awarded to MFS Network Technologies later this year.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
